### 3. Additional context (if relevant):
SCREENING METHODOLOGY:
- Conservative approach applied: studies with uncertain eligibility were included
- Age range flexibility: studies with age ranges slightly exceeding 6-11 years (e.g., 6-12, 8-12) were included if they 
contained target population
- Follow-up flexibility: studies with approximately 6 months follow-up (e.g., 20-24 weeks) were conservatively included
- Studies excluded primarily due to: non-RCT design, insufficient follow-up (<6 months), age outside range, or not 
targeting overweight/obese children

COMMON EXCLUSION REASONS:
1. Not an RCT (qualitative studies, systematic reviews, cohort studies, protocol papers) - 25 studies
2. Follow-up <6 months (most common reason for exclusion among RCTs) - 15 studies
3. Age outside 6-11 years (adolescents, infants, or general school populations) - 12 studies
4. Prevention studies rather than treatment of overweight/obese children - 5 studies
5. Non-obesity interventions (e.g., self-esteem, sleep, zinc supplementation) - 5 studies

INCLUDED STUDY TYPES:
- Family-based behavioral interventions (12 studies)
- School-based physical activity programs (8 studies)
- Parent-only interventions (6 studies)
- Diet and exercise combinations (7 studies)
- Multicomponent lifestyle interventions (5 studies)

NOTES FOR MANAGER:
- All 100 studies in the chunk (indices 201-300) have been screened
- 38 studies (38%) met inclusion criteria and should proceed to full-text review
- 62 studies (62%) were excluded at title/abstract stage
- No studies had low confidence ratings; all decisions were made with high or medium confidence
- Several borderline cases were conservatively included to avoid missing potentially eligible studies
